{number: 141}
{title: Savior, MoreThan Life to Me}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Savior, more than life to me,
I am [F] clinging, clinging [C] close to Thee;
Let Thy precious blood applied
Keep me [G7] ever, ever near Thy [C] side.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Every day, every hour,
Let me [F] feel Thy cleansing [C] pow'r;
May Thy tender love to me
Bind me [G7] closer, closer, Lord, to [C] Thee.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Through [C] this changing world below,
Lead me [F] gently, gently [C] as I go;
Trusting Thee, I cannot stray,
I can [G7] never, never lose my [C] way.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Let [C] me love Thee more and more,
Till this [F] fleeting, fleeting [C] life is o'er;
Till my soul is lost in love,
In a [G7] brighter, better world a-[C] bove.
{end_of_verse}
